    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d38">

                <pb facs="0052" n="32" xml:id="pg32"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 414.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 5, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As an evidence of the facility with which
                    the French government can borrow of its own citizens, and the ability of the
                    latter to lend, I enclose you a slip containing the report of the minister of
                    finance to his Majesty on the subject of the late loan.</p>
                <p>The buildings where the subscriptions were received were literally besieged for
                    hours before the time named for opening. France is no longer poor. It is a rich
                    country.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d38-a1.xml" xpointer="d38-a1"/>
            </div>
